    description: "The user-visible half of ADR-0047, and the leg the owner's ruling is conditioned on: 'yes as long as it's loud about it'.\n\nSCOPE.\n1. Overlays move INTO the package. docs/ is not in the wheel (pyproject: packages = [\"src/hypergumbo_core\"]), so the three overlays in docs/io-primitives-overlays/ cannot be loaded by an installed hypergumbo at all today.\n2. They load by DEFAULT, per language (INV-lufib: a claims-file overlay was once applied to every language and hard-failed any repo containing another).\n3. Each carries provenance: community, a dated retrieved:, so 'hypergumbo does not maintain these rows' is CHECKABLE rather than asserted.\n4. LOUD DISCLOSURE, ruling 6: catalog_provenance gains shipped_default / user_config layer keys AND a one-line stderr notice naming the overlays and their dates. A JSON field alone does NOT satisfy the ruling -- the shape to copy is the in_progress catalogue warning, which fires per queried language on every run.\n\nWHY user_supplied IS NOT ENOUGH: it is a boolean, and this ADR creates a THIRD state -- 'hypergumbo shipped it and does not vouch for it'. Collapsing that into either neighbour re-opens the INV-zosun gap."  # 7d21
    fields: {}  # 7d21
